{
  "sim_type": "excel",
  "title": "Titan Initiation Report: Synthesis and Price Target Defence",
  "scenario": "You are a junior analyst on a Mumbai equity desk completing Titan's initiation of coverage. Your senior has compiled the three-statement model, DCF, trading comps, and precedent-transaction analyses across separate sheets. Now you must synthesise the valuation outputs, compute the rating logic, and defend a price target in the one-page tearsheet that portfolio managers will actually read.",
  "instructions": "Build the initiation summary by synthesising the DCF, trading-comps, and precedent-transaction valuations into a football-field consensus, compute the price target, justify the rating, and populate the one-page summary metrics that defend your investment thesis on Titan.",
  "learning_objective": "Synthesise multiple valuation methods into a single price target, compute upside/downside logic to justify a rating, and populate the one-page initiation tearsheet that distils your entire research case into a PM-actionable summary.",
  "hints": [
    "The football field combines three valuation ranges weighted by method strength; start with the simple average of the three method midpoints, then refine by weighting.",
    "Rating logic: upside/downside % determines rating (>15% = Buy, −10% to +15% = Hold, <−10% = Sell). Compute the upside from current price to your target.",
    "The one-page tearsheet shows CMP, target, upside %, rating, FY25E financials (revenue, EBITDA, margin, PAT, EV/EBITDA), and the football-field valuation range in one tight summary."
  ],
